  "comments": "<p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">The first consignment of Namibian coins arrived at Walvis Bay on 13 November 1993, with official issuance to commercial banks commencing on 8 December 1993. The inaugural coin series included denominations of 5c, 10c, 50c, N$1.00, and N$5.00, each featuring designs inspired by Namibia’s rich fauna and flora. &nbsp;An uncirculated 1993 First Coinage booklet was issued, containing all five denominations, the exact number of these sets remains unknown.</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin-left:0px;\"><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/67c569c82143e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/67c569c82143e.jpg\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/67c569cb89557.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/67c569cb89557.jpg\"></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/67c569ceac41e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/67c569ceac41e.jpg\"></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Different mints were involved in production of this emission. As the result style varieties appeared.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br><br>Die <strong>1 </strong>- the script of date numerals tall and narrow.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - the script of date numerals wide.<br><br><i>Reverse</i><br><br>Die <strong>A</strong> - palm tree leaves close to rim.<br>Die <strong>B</strong> - palm tree leaves far from rim.<br><br><i>Combinations</i><br><strong>1</strong>+<strong>A</strong>: 1993, see photo below.<br><strong>1</strong>+<strong>B</strong>: 2002, 2007, 2012, 2015.<br><strong>2</strong>+<strong>B</strong>: 2009, see photo below.<br><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/611f7350adf76.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/611f7350adf76.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>From January 2019, the Bank of Namibia discontinued the production of the 5-cent coin. However, they still remain legal tender in Namibia.</p>",
